# Licensing

This repository contains three kinds of work, and they carry three different licences. **Replace the summary below with the full licence texts from the official sources before publishing** — GitHub only shows a licence badge when it can detect the full text of `LICENSE`.

| Part | Paths | Licence | Full text from |
|---|---|---|---|
| Software: host tools, firmware | `pwgd/`, `pwguard/`, `pwlib/`, `firmware/` | **Apache License 2.0** | https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.txt |
| Hardware: schematics, PCB, mechanical | `hardware/` | **CERN-OHL-S-2.0** (strongly reciprocal) | https://cern-ohl.web.cern.ch/ |
| Documentation | `README*.md`, `docs/`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `SECURITY.md` | **CC BY 4.0** | https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode |

Why these three:

- **Apache-2.0** for software: patent grant plus permissive reuse, so a commercial vendor can build a product without asking, while still being bound by the patent clause.
- **CERN-OHL-S** for hardware: strongly reciprocal, meaning anyone who ships a product based on these designs must publish their modified design files. For a security device, that reciprocity is the point — a closed derivative is a device nobody can audit.
- **CC BY 4.0** for documentation: maximum reach, minimal friction, attribution required.

---

## Notice to copy into design files

**Hardware (schematics, PCB, mechanical):**

```
Copyright (c) <year> <author>
This source describes Open Hardware and is licensed under the CERN-OHL-S v2.
You may redistribute and modify this source and make products using it under
the terms of the CERN-OHL-S v2 (https://cern-ohl.web.cern.ch/).
This source is distributed WITHOUT ANY EXPRESS OR IMPLIED WARRANTY, INCLUDING
OF MERCHANTABILITY, SATISFACTORY QUALITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
Please see the CERN-OHL-S v2 for applicable conditions.
Source location: <repository URL>
As per CERN-OHL-S v2 section 4, should You produce hardware based on this
source, You must where practicable maintain the Source Location visible on
the external case of the Gate or other products you make using this source.
```

**Software:**

```
Copyright (c) <year> <author>
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the "License");
you may not use this file except in compliance with the License.
You may obtain a copy of the License at
    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software
distributed under the License is distributed on an "AS IS" BASIS,
WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.
See the License for the specific language governing permissions and
limitations under the License.
```

